A||N||9||Capt Fiero||Update: Hot Rod 2.8 well not a 2.8 anymore.||||1||
Z||000000||Capt Fiero||10-16-2000||08:53 PM||||Under recomendations of my local machine shop the engine has been bored out to 2.9 with chromoly rings and roller tip rockers. I have set up a web page with all the listed mods, the shop ran it through desktop dyno and came up with 190hp at 6000rpms and 192lbs of torqu at 4500rpms. But take a quick peek at the page for a full list of mods.    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/capt_fiero2000/capts_page.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/capt_fiero2000/capts_page.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>Under Constuction||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||10-16-2000||09:36 PM||||Can you give the camshaft specifications so that I could run the numbers on my Dyno2000 program and than use that to figure out what the 1/4-mile and 0-60 times would be? If you don't know them than could you just give me the manufacturer name and part numbers of the camshaft. I also need to know if your heads are ported or not.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||10-16-2000||09:59 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.federalmogul.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.federalmogul.com/</A>   the cam is the pro 2000, sorry I do not have the specs as the machine shop took the cam spec card for there own testing. The heads are polished and a 3 angle valve grind done to them.  ||||reg||1
