Z||000004||80's BOY||10-17-2000||10:47 AM||||how does the car idle WITH THE 19# injectors?? is it driveable without the juice, or is it race only? just wondering because i have the same mods without nitrous and those injectors sucked for me.||||reg||5
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||10-17-2000||10:57 AM||||That's some wild power for a bored 2.8. My 3.2 project is only projected at 170hp and 205 ftlbs of torque, of course I didn't use a very wild cam (going for a torquey engine) but still, if you can push a 2.9 that hard w/o nitrous that's really sweet.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||10-17-2000||11:34 AM||||nice looking car! you'll LOVE the nitrous! is there a Dynojet near you? <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  run your can and see what she lay down with and without NO2. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||10-17-2000||05:14 PM||||Well I don't have camshaft specifications for Speed Pro camshafts but I have specifications for just about everything else. I went to the Federal Mogul web-sight and only found a description on the camshaft and the rpm range. I ran some numbers anyway with a camshaft I think might be similar to the one you have. I used the Comp Cams 2030, which has 204/214 duration, .423/. 423 lift and a 109-degree lobe separation angle. The power output I got with ported fiero heads is 175 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 196-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500-4000 rpm. Without ported heads I got 165 horsepower @ 5000-5500 rpm and 194-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm. I took into consideration your ported manifolds, which is considered high performance manifolds and I used a 3.560” bore and 2.99” stroke crankshaft. I have the flow bench data for the fiero heads ported and unported which will give you a more accurate simulation than using the pull down menu’s from the program.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Capt Fiero||10-17-2000||06:14 PM||||Ok, now I want to find out why the numbers are diffrent than what the machine shop told me, They used 450cfm for throttle body air flow. 6500rpms for "redline" (I know the stock chip stops me before 6250, I am going to get a new chip)  Could you send me a screen shot of the program so that I can see what variables there are.  send it to captfieroofbc@home.com <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>Under Constuction||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||10-17-2000||10:45 PM||||The difference between 450 cfm and 500 cfm, which is what I used, is 1 peak horsepower and two-ft. lbs. of torque. The numbers are different because I typed in the head flow numbers into the program directly for the fiero heads. Your machinist may have just used the head type drop down menus from the program. The menu has universal head flow data that has flow numbers built into the program that don't reflect the amount of air the fiero heads actually flow. I don't have the same camshaft specifications in my dyno that your machinist has so that also makes a big difference.<P>I will send you that file and if you give me those camshaft specifications I will give you an accurate simulation of your engine as well as what your car could run in the quarter mile and your 0-60 time.<P>||||reg||1
